    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0280" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/368</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moser</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-23T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1918,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>Ambassador, Vologda, requests that Emerson be sent immediately with two to five
                    engineers to Vologda to confer about transportation. Ambassador promises special
                    car and safe-conduct. Department approves. Advise Ambassador when Emerson can
                    leave, notifying the Department at same time. If absence of Emerson would
                    interfere with your work on Chinese Eastern send next best man available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
